---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../components/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Is $400 a lot for a balayage?",
    answer: "Yes, for a standard full balayage in NZ. The highest starting price on the eight NZ salon price lists checked was $365. Very long or thick hair, a big colour change or a senior stylist can push a price higher, so ask what's included before you compare."
  },
  {
    question: "What is a full head balayage?",
    answer: "It's balayage painted through the whole head, rather than only the top layers or the pieces around your face. Some salons also list a half head balayage for less. Melissa's balayage is one service at $280, and she'll talk through placement at your appointment."
  },
  {
    question: "Does balayage cost more than foils?",
    answer: "It depends on how many foils you're comparing it with. At Hair By Melissa, balayage and a full head of foils are both $280. Half head foils are $200 and partial foils are $150."
  },
  {
    question: "How long does a balayage appointment take?",
    answer: "Allow 3 to 4 hours at Hair By Melissa. Longer or thicker hair can take more time, and Melissa will confirm this at your consultation."
  },
  {
    question: "How long does balayage last?",
    answer: "There's no fixed date, because balayage grows out softly without a hard regrowth line. If you like to keep the contrast fresh, plan on every 8 to 12 weeks. Plenty of people leave it longer and come back when they're ready."
  }
];
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title="How Much Does Balayage Cost in NZ?"
  description="Full balayage is usually about $250 to $340 at Auckland salons. What changes the price, what to check is included, and what $280 gets you in Kaukapakapa."
  keywords="balayage cost nz, how much does balayage cost, balayage price nz, how long does balayage last, balayage north auckland"
  slug="balayage-cost-nz"
  h1="How Much Does Balayage Cost in NZ?"
  crumb="Balayage Cost NZ"
  category="Colour Insights"
  readTime="5 min read"
  publishDate="2026-11-06"
  displayDate="6 November 2026"
  intro="Balayage is a colour technique where highlights are hand-painted onto your hair, so they grow out softly. A full balayage usually costs about $250 to $340 at an Auckland salon. At Hair By Melissa in Kaukapakapa, North Auckland, it's $280 and takes 3 to 4 hours."
  quickAnswer="Expect about $250 to $340 for a full balayage in Auckland. Many of those are 'from' prices, and some salons charge for toner on top, so compare what's included as well as the number. Melissa's balayage is $280."
  imageAlt="Illustration: long caramel balayage hair, seen from behind, in a bright salon chair"
  faqs={faqs}
  ctaHeading="Thinking about balayage?"
  ctaText="Balayage with Melissa is $280, one-on-one, with free parking at the door in Kaukapakapa."
  related={[
    { href: "/services/balayage/", title: "Balayage in Kaukapakapa", text: "What's included, how long it takes and how to look after it." },
    { href: "/blog/balayage-vs-highlights/", title: "Balayage vs Highlights", text: "How the two techniques differ, and which suits you." },
    { href: "/blog/half-head-vs-full-head-foils/", title: "Half Head vs Full Head Foils", text: "Foil prices and how much of your head you really need done." }
  ]}
>
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What does balayage cost in New Zealand?</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Eight NZ salon price lists, checked in November 2026, show most Auckland salons between about $250 and $340 for a full balayage. Here's how that looks by area.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-200 text-left text-gray-700">
        <caption class="sr-only">Published full balayage prices at NZ salons, November 2026</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-gray-50">
            <th scope="col" class="border border-gray-200 p-3 font-semibold">Where</th>
            <th scope="col" class="border border-gray-200 p-3 font-semibold">Published price</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="border border-gray-200 p-3 font-semibold align-top">Auckland salons</th>
            <td class="border border-gray-200 p-3 align-top">About $250 to $340</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="border border-gray-200 p-3 font-semibold align-top">Hamilton</th>
            <td class="border border-gray-200 p-3 align-top">From $295, toner extra</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="border border-gray-200 p-3 font-semibold align-top">Wellington</th>
            <td class="border border-gray-200 p-3 align-top">From $365</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row" class="border border-gray-200 p-3 font-semibold align-top">Hair By Melissa, Kaukapakapa</th>
            <td class="border border-gray-200 p-3 align-top">$280</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Treat these as a guide. Salons change their prices, and a lower number isn't always cheaper once the extras are added.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What changes the price of balayage?</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-3">
      <li><strong>Your hair.</strong> Longer or thicker hair takes more time to paint, process and style.</li>
      <li><strong>The stylist.</strong> Some salons price by experience level, so the same service can cost more with a senior stylist.</li>
      <li><strong>Toner.</strong> Some salons include it. Others charge for it separately, which can add a real amount to the bill.</li>
      <li><strong>Extra colour or bond products.</strong> Some salons add a charge for these.</li>
      <li><strong>The finish.</strong> A few salons ask you to book a cut or blow wave alongside your colour.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What to ask before you book</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">A quick message to the salon saves a surprise at the end. Ask:</p>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
      <li>Is that price fixed, or is it a 'from' price?</li>
      <li>Is toner included?</li>
      <li>Is a blow wave or finish included?</li>
      <li>Does longer or thicker hair cost more?</li>
      <li>How long should I allow?</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What you get for $280 at Hair By Melissa</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      It's you and Melissa, one client at a time, in a quiet home salon on Magnolia Lane. Your appointment starts with a chat about the look you want. Melissa then hand-paints the colour, tones it and finishes your hair so you can see the result properly. <a href="/services/balayage/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">Here's the full balayage service</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Allow 3 to 4 hours. Longer or thicker hair can take more time, and Melissa will confirm that at your consultation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Is balayage better value than foils?</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      At Melissa's, balayage and a full head of foils cost the same: $280. The difference shows up later. Foils usually need redoing every 6 to 8 weeks, while balayage grows out softly, so you can go longer between visits. If you want a smaller change, <a href="/services/partial-foils/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">partial foils</a> are $150 and <a href="/services/half-head-highlights/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">half head foils</a> are $200.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Wondering which suits your hair? The <a href="/blog/balayage-vs-highlights/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">balayage vs highlights guide</a> walks through it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
    Prices are from published NZ salon price lists, checked 6 November 2026. They may have changed since.
  </p>
</BlogPostLayout>
